	(descr "XKB Industrial Precision XKNANO-113 nano-SIM push-push socket, LCSC C381071. Task 14c re-pick (replaces JXTCONN CSIM-H137-7P, LCSC C42420236, which had no retrievable EasyEDA CAD and an unconfirmed CD polarity). GEOMETRY from the LCSC/EasyEDA C381071 verified land pattern (easyeda2kicad --full): 7 small SMD contact pads (VCC/RST/CLK/CD/GND/VPP/IO, 0.6-0.8x1.3mm at y=-6.74) + 4 large SMD shell tabs (1.0x2.1mm at the four corners, all renumbered pad 8 to merge onto one symbol pin, matching this project's MHF4 GND-tab convention) + 2 unnamed 0.9mm NPTH mounting pegs (no signal, listed in check_footprints.py REVERSE_ALLOWLIST). CD polarity CONFIRMED from XKB's own drawing (Dwg No. XKNANO-113, LCSC datasheet mirror): CD switch to GND reads NORMAL=SHORT / CARD INSERTED=OPEN -- matches this project's \"grounded=absent\" DET convention (verification.md Item 7) exactly, closing the open CD-polarity order gate from docs/sourcing.md Sec.5 Note 3 with a documented answer.")
	(tags "SIM nanoSIM UICC push-push connector XKB XKNANO-113")
